42.8s 50 Self-selected decisions:
42.8s 51 - Self-selected: R0 and R2 test the lemma's exact standardisation (no epsilon); the pipeline's N keeps eps = 1e-6 from frozen v1.0, and its deviation from N o A = N is printed, not asserted.
42.8s 52 - Self-selected: target-condition noise is a seeded numpy float32 field in 32-image blocks; the same blocks feed the pixel identification and every encoder. Source-side noise (degraded A2, AutoEval meta-sets) comes from a seeded torch generator on the device, one field per batch shared across blur levels.
42.8s 53 - Self-selected: pixel DCTs use scipy.fft (type II, orthonormal) and a sparse binning matrix, both asserted equal to the v1.0 matrix and bincount reference (<= 1e-9 relative).
42.8s 54 - Self-selected: knee fits use the SSE-by-expansion form and the v1.1 tail fit is vectorised by valid-level pattern; both are asserted against the v1.0 reference on random curves (>= 98% identical grid indices).
42.8s 55 - Self-selected: R1 and R10 use the closed form int_0^eta Var_{pi_u}(lambda) du = E_{pi_0}[lambda] - E_{pi_eta}[lambda] (log-partition identity), so they test the identity rather than quadrature error; O_x keeps the frozen 32-point trapezoid.
42.8s 56 - Self-selected: pooled statistics weight datasets equally (mean of per-dataset means), matching the hierarchical bootstrap that resamples datasets first; the addendum's regime statistics average a dataset's seeds before pooling.
42.8s 57 - Self-selected: COT and COTT use the A2 label marginal as the source label distribution and solve the C x n transportation problem, asserted equal to the n x n assignment on random cases; the target transport costs are computed once per condition and shared by the baselines and the plug-ins (same random streams, so COT and COTT equal their run-1 definitions).
42.8s 58 - Self-selected: NucNorm accuracy comes from a LinearRegression of accuracy on the normalised nuclear norm over the AutoEval meta-sets; the ICML 2023 paper reports correlations only.
42.8s 59 - Self-selected: predictions from regressions and confidence differences (DoC, the AutoEval family, NucNorm, DoC@s_hat, COT@s_hat, AE-LS+s_hat) are clipped to [0, 1]; this can only lower their error.
42.8s 60 - Self-selected: PT_anchor weights are fitted once per target subset, because the anchor features at s = 256 px^2 do not depend on a condition's blur or noise.
42.8s 61 - Self-selected: the mechanism screen runs on the 120 target tiles per dataset only; the knee rho uses no source tiles, which would cost about 45 GPU-minutes without entering any rule.
42.8s 62 - Self-selected: stress tests (noise sweep, PSF misspecification, JPEG) run on a random subsample of at most 240 B images per dataset; the v1.0 check uses the full A2 calibration split, the v2 noise-model check at most 240 A2 images.
42.8s 63 - Self-selected: images (and LandCover.ai tiles) whose minimum per-channel std is below 0.5 DN are dropped (logged for images), because a constant channel makes the normalised response undefined.
42.8s 64 - Self-selected: the six method encoders stay in CPU RAM and move to the GPU one at a time, which avoids about 150 reloads while keeping one encoder on the GPU.
42.8s 65 - Self-selected: in the certificate experiment an abstention counts as a coverage failure, and n_Q = 'all' is a single repetition on the full B.
42.8s 66 - Self-selected: in MODE=full a failed check_figure triggers tick thinning and a re-check; a remaining problem is logged in the manifest instead of aborting after the GPU blocks. In DRY_RUN the check is strict.
42.8s 67 - Self-selected: DRY_RUN writes to outputs_dryrun/ and its checkpoints carry a dry-run flag, so a smoke test can never be resumed into a real run.
42.8s 68 - Self-selected: one universal session budget (REDEG_BUDGET_H, default 11 h, measured from the first cell) replaces the projection-based dropping of run 1, which dropped all seed replication on a warm-up throughput estimate: units run in a fixed order (B2, B3, B4, B5, B6), each unit part (pixel stage, one encoder pass, one mechanism unit) starts only if its live estimate fits before the compute stop (budget minus a 0.25 h packaging reserve), and nothing is dropped; once the budget is used up an IPython input transformer replaces every later cell by a one-line skip notice, except the cells marked @always-run (inventory, completeness, packaging, final cell).
42.8s 69 - Self-selected: the analyses (Sections 7-9, marked @needs-complete) run in the session that finishes every compute unit; a session that ends with pending units only packages its checkpoints, so no partial result can be mistaken for the final one.
42.8s 70 - Self-selected: a session acquires only the datasets its pending units read; data-dependent assumption checks of an earlier session are kept when no dataset is loaded.
42.8s 71 - Self-selected: throughput measured during the self-check is discarded and a measured rate is trusted only after 2,000 images, because warm-up passes made run 1 overestimate the run by a factor of three.
42.8s 72 - Self-selected: resume searches every attached input up to 7 folder levels deep for checkpoint folders and zip files (Kaggle may keep or extract an uploaded zip); zips are opened in DATA_DIR and only checkpoint files are read; inputs are reported as anonymous '<input #k>' labels, never by dataset slug or owner.
42.8s 73 - Self-selected: checkpoints of run 1 (frozen v1.0, no addendum hash) are reused only for units whose computation the addendum leaves unchanged (B1 and the B5 mechanism units); B2 gains the Fig. 1(b) curves, B3, B4 and B6 gain the addendum estimators, and B5_vicreg_r50 is recomputed because run 1 loaded Barlow Twins weights for VICReg.
42.8s 74 - Self-selected: Barlow Twins and VICReg weights are downloaded under distinct cache names, and every encoder's weight fingerprint (parameter count, sum of |theta|) must differ from every other encoder's.
42.8s 75 - Self-selected: COT@s_hat = acc_src(level) + COT_err_src(level) - COT_err_target (the COT error calibrated on the re-degraded source, DoC-style); COTT@s_hat refits the COTT threshold on A2 at the level with the true A2 labels.
42.8s 76 - Self-selected: the v2 noise-model check simulates A2 at (s_v11, sigma_v11) by adding fresh Gaussian noise in the orthonormal DCT domain (equal in distribution to pixel-space white noise) on at most 480 A2 images per condition.
42.8s 77 - Self-selected: the GSD chain for LandCover.ai 25 -> 50 cm is calibrated on 300 A2 tiles over CHAIN_GRID = {0} U geomspace(0.05, 64, 20) and applied to all A2 tiles per condition; the chain outputs are cached across the six encoder passes of the unit.
42.8s 78 - Self-selected: the addendum adds PatternNet <-> RESISC45 (shared class names after the I-10 normalisation) to the real shifts; together with seeds 1-2 these are data run 1 never used, and every addendum rule also reports its verdict on that fresh subset.
42.8s 79 - Self-selected: the lean zip carries unit checkpoints (parts only for unfinished units), figures (PDF + PNG), tables (TeX + CSV), key_results.txt, run_manifest.json and a resume note; logs, figure data and code stay in OUTPUT_DIR. Text outputs pass an anonymity audit (input paths, e-mail addresses, home folders) before zipping.
