42.8s 92 - Self-selected: in T13 the real-shift column marks the registered non-inferiority criterion of P3 (dagger) instead of a significance test; Fig. 7 draws the 95% CIs as thin bars below each row so that they never hide the change arrows, and omits arrows too short to draw.
42.8s 93 - Self-selected (v3): the nine corruptions are re-implemented in numpy/scipy/PIL (no OpenCV or ImageMagick), and Cell 5.6 compares every family and severity with the reference package imagecorruptions 1.1.2 on the same random draws (identical uint8 outputs required). ImageNet-C's glass-blur 'swap' acts on numpy views and therefore copies x[h', w'] into x[h, w]; the re-implementation keeps exactly that behaviour.
42.8s 94 - Self-selected (v3): each corrupted image draws from its own keyed stream (dataset, split, family, severity, image), so a corruption is reproducible and independent of the thread pool; the corrupted copies of A2 and B are computed once per dataset, cached outside OUTPUT_DIR for the six encoder passes, and regenerated with a checksum check when a later session resumes a unit.
42.8s 95 - Self-selected (v3): block B9 caps A2 and B at 400 images per dataset (keyed subsample) so that ten datasets x 46 conditions x six encoders fit one session; A1 (the probe's training split) is the full B3 split.
42.8s 96 - Self-selected (v3): ATC@NR uses the variance of the Laplacian, fixed in advance as the most widely used classic no-reference blur metric; both no-reference metrics are computed from the DCT spectrum (the 3x3 Laplacian with reflect boundary is diagonalised by the DCT-II), and Cell 5.6 asserts agreement with scipy.ndimage.laplace.
42.8s 97 - Self-selected (v3): SpaceNet MVOI uses the panchromatic band (all 27 views on one 0.5 m grid), stretched linearly per view between the 0.1 and 99.9 percentiles of its selected tiles and replicated to three channels; 48 tiles whose 16 crops are valid (<= 1% no-data, non-flat) in all 27 views are taken in a keyed order and split 16/16/16 into probe, calibration and target tiles.
42.8s 98 - Self-selected (v3): building footprints (longitude/latitude) are projected to the tiles' UTM zone with a Krueger-series transverse Mercator (agrees with PROJ to below 0.1 mm) and rasterised on the tile grid read from the GeoTIFF tags; a crop shows a building when footprints cover at least 2% of it. If fewer than 90% of the footprint vertices fall inside their tiles, the accuracy part of B11 is skipped and reported, while the pixel-only part still runs.
42.8s 99 - Self-selected (v3): B10 rebuilds the B3 seed-0 conditions from the keyed streams and reports whether their median knees equal the B3 checkpoints, so the no-reference metrics are evaluated on exactly the conditions of the published comparison.
